      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure how this was working before without a cast to uint32_t, but `vrndnq_f32` would have the same problem since they round to an integral floating point value, not an actual bitwise integer that `pixel_round_as_RP` is meant to return.\n\nI\u0027m also not sure about wholesale disabling the use of a scalar function when it\u0027s supposedly available for an architecture that we are not otherwise supporting or testing. What is the context for `vrndnq_f32` being more supported than `vrndns_f32`?",
